From a705b7e67b090fbbd8a9f0cac9a430de3bd95d2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:57:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] device: clear actions use the SurfaceFlinger GC16 clear

The clear key action, the Clear Screen tile and EINK_FORCE_CLEAR now
call SurfaceFlinger transaction 1113 (GC16, repaint, release after
present) through the existing worker-thread command runner. The key
action no longer switches to Regal and adds black/white overlay windows
(which ran in the app waveform), and the daemon's force-and-sleep "r"
command, which never requested a repaint, is removed.

The daemon also drops "c" (the former Regal clear command) and its refresh-mode table; it now handles only lights, au_br, an_fl, clean and scroll. The EINK_* control broadcasts no longer exist.
